# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the FFmpeg tests (used by the thread-sanitizer preset only).
# FFmpeg's shared libraries are not instrumented: libavcodec's slice and frame threads synchronize
# their own buffers with primitives ThreadSanitizer cannot see (atomics and progress flags in the
# uninstrumented code), so valid decoding is reported as races between FFmpeg's threads (memset,
# free and av_buffer writes inside libavcodec and libavutil), and as races with the dvv code that
# reads a decoded frame after FFmpeg has handed it over. A report is suppressed when the stack of
# either racing access (or of the allocation of the memory) has a frame inside these libraries, so a
# race between dvv code and FFmpeg is hidden as well; races between two accesses in dvv code are
# still reported.
race:libavcodec.so
race:libavutil.so
